      <activity id="2389f6cb-f961-526e-937d-de02556351ee" activityNameId="9651c664-c33b-53e5-a047-98d3e866ca28" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electricity, at cogen 50kWth, wood pellets, allocation exergy</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electricity, at cogen 50kWth, wood pellets, allocation exergy
Inventory for 1 MJ heat from pellets, burned in a cogeneration unit with a capacity of 50 kWth. The multioutput process "pellets, burned in cogen 50kWth delivers the coproducts "heat, at cogen 50kWth, pellets, allocation exergy" and "electricity, at cogen 50kWth, pellets, allocation exergy". The energy efficiency is 26% for electricity and 65% for heat. The exergy factor is 1 for ectricity and 0.164 for heat. This leads to the allocation factor of 0.71 for electricity an 0.29 for heat.
Included are the pellets burning in a 50 kWth cogen unit which in turn includes fuel input, infrastructure (boiler), air and water emissions and electrictiy needed for operation. The efficiency and allocation according to exergy is considered
Location: Data apply to the combustion in Switzerland. 
Technology: efficiency of average technology available on the market
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: none
Sampling: Data from literature
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_acdc97b3-2168-3309-a515-6c7562b328f5.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
